### Java Utility Classes: StringTokenizer, Formatter, Scanner & Console

- **`StringTokenizer` (`java.util`):** Breaks a string into tokens based on specified delimiters (default whitespace). Methods: `hasMoreTokens()`, `nextToken()`, `countTokens()`.
- **`Formatter` (`java.util`):** Formats text using C-style `printf` specifiers (`%s`, `%d`, `%f`, `%t`).
- **`Scanner` (`java.util`):** Parses primitive types and strings using regular expressions from console or files (`nextInt()`, `nextLine()`).
- **`Console` (`java.io`):** Directly accesses system console with password masking (`readPassword()`).

```java
StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer("Java,OOPJ,2026", ",");
while (st.hasMoreTokens()) {
    System.out.println(st.nextToken());
}
```

$$\therefore \text{Utility classes provide parsing, text formatting, and secure terminal interaction.}$$
